# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.

# --- Early-access waitlist (app/api/waitlist/route.ts) -----------------------

# Required. Create at https://resend.com/api-keys
# Without it the endpoint returns 503 and logs the lead rather than losing it.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Optional. Where early-access requests land.
# This one MUST be a real, monitored mailbox - it is the only record of a lead.
# Defaults to marketing@stafflyconsulting.com
WAITLIST_TO=

# Optional. The From address, i.e. the sender label on the notification.
# The mailbox does NOT need to exist; what Resend requires is that the DOMAIN is
# verified there (one-time SPF/DKIM DNS setup). A noreply@ with no inbox is fine:
# the route sets Reply-To to the applicant, so hitting Reply reaches them, never
# this address. Bounces go to Resend's own return path, not here.
#
# Defaults to Resend's shared test sender, which works with no DNS setup but has
# poor deliverability - verify stafflyconsulting.com and switch to your own address.
# Example: "Staffly ATS+ <noreply@stafflyconsulting.com>"
WAITLIST_FROM=
